    reg {
        name = "VHD vertical luminance scaling/filtering coefficient register";
        desc = "VHDVLCOEF is a VHD vertical luminance scaling/filtering coefficient register. For details about the storage format, see the description of the VHDHLCOEF register. The VHD vertical luminance scaling coefficients have six taps and 32 phases. As the coefficients are symmetrical, there are 17 groups of coefficients. That is, 4-tap coefficients of phases 0-16 are stored. Each register address has two 10-bit coefficients. Therefore, four 32-bit register addresses are required for storing the 6-tap coefficients of each phase.

Data sheet 11.2.4 VHDVLCOEF (offset 0xD400, printed page 11-264, `datasheet.txt` line 47898).";

        field {
            name = "vlcoefn2";
            desc = "Vertical luminance scaling/filtering coefficient. Indicates the tap-2 coefficients when bit[3:0] of the register address are 0x0. Indicate the tap-4 coefficients when bits[3:0] of the register address are 0x4. Indicates the tap-6 coefficients when bits[3:0] of the register address are 0x8. Indicates a reserved field when bits[3:0] of the register address is 0xC.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vlcoefn2[25:16];

        field {
